e capone's death capone had  the mental capacity of a 12-year-old  we're then introduced to capone's friend  johnny he's invited down by may  likely in an attempt to cheer capone up  and have him be around familiar faces  just like the doctor ordered the strange  thing about johnny is that we the viewer  aren't sure if what we're seeing is real  or not in this way we're made to feel  just like capone although mae is the one  to invite him down we never see him  interact with her we see capone having a  drink with johnny but when may asks him  who he's talking to  no one is there perhaps only the first  two scenes with him  actually happened or perhaps none at all  johnny becomes this specter of capone's  past  life he tells capone how grateful he is  for taking him off the street and it's  revealed he was the one  tortured and stabbed by geno for  skimming cash off the top  and allegedly working with the feds like  many of the characters in this film  johnny isn't based off a real life  person the only significant  johnny in al capone's life was johnny  torrio who was his mentor but he died of  a heart attack and was significantly  older than al  in one of the more gruesome scenes of  the film johnny scoops out his eyes  telling capone the key to the money can  be found in these  the eyeballs are placed directly looking  at him the key is inside of him  in his mind the tragedy is that he can't  reach it capone watches the wizard of oz  and sings the cowardly lions if  i were king of the forest he literally  has the lion's face projected onto him a  shell of the lion he once was  in the wizard of oz the cowardly lion is  looking for courage and courage is a big  theme in capone  capone tells johnny maybe if yeah had  some coverage  you might be able to find yourself some  new friends  and earlier when geno kills johnny he  says where's your [ __ ] courage now  capone himself does not have the courage  to confront his past specifically his  son  it isn't until the end